Rule 1 (t and e must have the same data type)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 2 (t and e are pairwise broadcastable when ranks match)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)) ∨ (shape(v_1, i) = 1) ∨ (shape(v_2, i) = 1)
>>
Rule 3 (condition is broadcastable to t)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)) ∨ (shape(v_1, i) = 1)
>>
Rule 5 (either all input ranks are equal or the condition is a scalar)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_2) = ndim(v_3)) ∨ (ndim(v_1) = 0)
>>
Rule 6 (zero-size dimension compatibility between t and e when ranks match)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : if (shape(v_1, i) = 0 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 0) then shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 7 (name is a free string parameter)
{v_1 : str} |= v_1 = v_1
